<headroom-library version="1" id="crunch-treble-boosted-plexi" category="Crunch" order="120" instrument="guitar" style="Classic Rock">
  <description>A germanium treble booster slamming the front of a 100-watt plexi: the late-60s/early-70s British lead bite. The booster cuts the bass and drives the amp's top end into a cutting, vocal crunch that thickens humbuckers and makes single coils scream. Ease the boost for rhythm.</description>
  <tags><tag>Crunch</tag><tag>Classic Rock</tag><tag>Treble Booster</tag><tag>Lead</tag><tag>Humbucker</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dallas_Rangemaster_Treble_Booster" title="Dallas Rangemaster Treble Booster (Wikipedia)"/>
